$(1)$ If $z$ is the unique closed $\kk$-point of $Z_1$ then $\gamma_{Z_1}(\cO_z) \cong \cO_X \cong \pi_*\cO_	X$. 
oindent$(2)$ Let $z \in Z_2$ be a closed $\kk$-point and let $\cE_z := \gamma_{Z_2}(\cO_z) \in  D(X)$ be the corresponding object. Then  egin{itemize} \item[(a)] if the component of $Z_2$ containing $z$ is reduced and corresponds to the $i$-th blowup center, then  egin{equation*} \cE_z \cong \pi_*\cO_	X(h-e_i); \end{equation*} \item[(b)] if the component of $Z_2$ containing $z$ has length $2$ then  egin{equation*} \cE_z \cong \pi_*\cO_	X(h-e_1) \cong \pi_*\cO_	X(h - e_2); \end{equation*} \item[(c)] if the component of $Z_2$ containing $z$ has length $3$, then  egin{equation*} \cE_z \cong \pi_*\cO_	X(h-e_1) \cong \pi_*\cO_	X(h - e_2) \cong \pi_*\cO_	X(h - e_3). \end{equation*} \end{itemize} 
oindent$(3)$ Let $z \in Z_3$ be a closed $\kk$-point and let $\cE_z := \gamma_{Z_3}(\cO_z) \in  D(X)$ be the corresponding object. Then  egin{itemize} \item[(a)] if the component of $Z_3$ containing $z$ is reduced then  egin{equation*} \cE_z \cong \pi_*\cO_	X(h) \qquad	ext{or}\qquad \cE_z \cong \pi_*\cO_	X(2h - e_1 - e_2 - e_3); \end{equation*} \item[(b)] if the component of $Z_3$ containing $z$ has length $2$ then  egin{equation*} \cE_z \cong \pi_*\cO_	X(h) \cong \pi_*\cO_	X(2h - e_1 - e_2 - e_3). \end{equation*} \end{itemize} In all these cases, $\cE_z$ is a globally generated sheaf, and if $z \in Z_d$ then  egin{equation*} \dim H^0(X,\cE_z) = d \qquand H^{i}(X,\cE_z) = 0 \quad	ext{for $i 
